// COVERS M3LexerGrammar: let, allVersions
//
// Expression-level Pure. `let` is the one that matters: the stress corpus is 30+ files and
// 89 services and has never written a local variable, because every generated function body
// is a single chained expression.
//
// `toBytes` is NOT declared here, and the reason is worth recording. Writing `$s->toBytes()`
// in a function body parses -- but it lexes as an ordinary function call, not as M3's
// TO_BYTES token, which is reachable only from `primitiveValueAtomic` (test parameters and
// EqualTo expected values). Declaring it here would have been a false credit that this
// harness could not detect, since the COVERS check only proves the text is present. It is
// covered by service-testsuite.pure instead, in a position where the token is really used.
//
// `allVersionsInRange` is absent for a harder reason: DomainParseTreeWalker.java:1742
// throws unconditionally. The branch exists only to reject -- `allVersions` on the line
// above maps to getAllVersions. It is in ../negative/ with the rest of the surface
// legend-engine declares and refuses.
###Pure
Class <<meta::pure::profiles::temporal.businesstemporal>> fixture::m3::Product
{
   name: String[1];
   size: Integer[1];
}

function fixture::m3::withLet(limit: Integer[1]): Integer[1]
{
   let offset = $limit + 10;
   let doubled = $offset * 2;
   $doubled;
}

function fixture::m3::everyVersion(): meta::pure::metamodel::type::Any[*]
{
   fixture::m3::Product.allVersions()
}
